 r←Test_05_BadTransaction base_url;after;before;h;payload;res
⍝ Send a POST where second row violates a NOT NULL constraint (empty `type` → NULL bind → server-side rejection).
⍝ Transact error-guard: the first row's insert must be rolled back, and the HTTP response shows the SQAPL/server error message.

 before←#.DCMS.SQL.Do'SELECT COUNT(*) FROM event_type'

 payload←'[{"type":"good_type","description":"row 1 should be rolled back","url_slug":"tx-test-1"},{"type":"","description":"row 2 forces NOT NULL violation","url_slug":"tx-test-2"}]'

 h←⎕NEW #.HttpCommand'POST'
 h.URL←base_url,'/crud/event_type'
 'x-api-key'h.SetHeader #.DCMS.GLOBAL.secrets.upload_token
 h.ContentType←'application/json'
 h.Params←payload
 res←h.Run

 after←#.DCMS.SQL.Do'SELECT COUNT(*) FROM event_type'

 res←0⎕json res.Data
 r←after≡before
 r∧←res.error≡500
 r∧←'cannot be null'(∨/⍷)res.message
